\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Overall effectiveness on CPU benchmark suites across five heterogeneous CPU hosts (M1--M5). \textsc  {BenchScout}\xspace  {} rows use the full pipeline: router Top-$K$, \emph  {probe-model-predicted} partial scores, and reconstruction (Section\nonbreakingspace \ref {subsec:overall-effectiveness}). Wang-style DNN and Tousi-style MLP rows are local execution-free proxies inspired by\nonbreakingspace \citep  {wang2019predicting,tousi2022comparative}, using static hardware features only; they are not reproductions of the cited methods. PTS-CPU proxy errors use the same log-mean targets and run-held-out folds as \textsc  {BenchScout}\xspace  {}. Time is an estimated new-measurement budget in seconds: zero for history, about 3.5\,s for static-feature collection, and 18.0--18.1\,s for BenchScout context plus selected probes. Full-suite entries are historical wall times, not paired timing controls. Bold marks the lowest error in each host column.}}{7}{table.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:overall-effectiveness-cpu}{{3}{7}{Overall effectiveness on CPU benchmark suites across five heterogeneous CPU hosts (M1--M5). \ourmethod {} rows use the full pipeline: router Top-$K$, \emph {probe-model-predicted} partial scores, and reconstruction (Section~\ref {subsec:overall-effectiveness}). Wang-style DNN and Tousi-style MLP rows are local execution-free proxies inspired by~\cite {wang2019predicting,tousi2022comparative}, using static hardware features only; they are not reproductions of the cited methods. PTS-CPU proxy errors use the same log-mean targets and run-held-out folds as \ourmethod {}. Time is an estimated new-measurement budget in seconds: zero for history, about 3.5\,s for static-feature collection, and 18.0--18.1\,s for BenchScout context plus selected probes. Full-suite entries are historical wall times, not paired timing controls. Bold marks the lowest error in each host column}{table.caption.33}{}}
